            <ArticleTitle>Case report: quetiapine and refractory hypotension during general anesthesia in the operating room.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>641-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1213/ANE.0b013e3182999689</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Quetiapine is an atypical antipsychotic with known α-adrenergic antagonism. We present a case of refractory hypotension that occurred after induction of general anesthesia in a patient being treated with quetiapine. This patient was not currently taking antihypertensives and had no known cardiovascular abnormalities. We observed that the hypotension was most responsive to vasopressin. We recommend further investigation regarding the interaction of quetiapine and general anesthesia.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
